+| `VK/VKTextureCache.cpp` (`upload_image_from_cpu`) | `r2gx::texpack_upload()` before `vk::upload_image`, behind one `bool` test. |
+| `CMakeLists.txt` | `VKR2Gfx.cpp` added to `rpcs3_rsx`. |
+| `VK/VKPipelineCompiler.cpp/.h`, `VK/VKGSRender.cpp`, `port_r2memo.h` | Round 10: `R2_VK_PIPE_CACHE` (default on) seeds the shared `VkPipelineCache` from `shaders_cache/vk_pipeline_cache.bin` (checked against vendor/device/pipelineCacheUUID, `pipe_cache_header_ok`) and writes it back after the preload and in `destroy_pipe_compiler`; the driver only skips back-end compilation, pipelines are identical. Pipelines linked after the preload are logged as disk-cache misses. |
+| `VK/VKPipelineCompiler.cpp/.h`, `VK/VKProgramPipeline.cpp/.h`, `VK/vkutils/device.cpp/.h`, `VK/VKGSRender.cpp`, `VK/VKR2Pipe.cpp/.h`, `VK/VKR2Fossilize.cpp/.h`, `rsx_cache.h`, `Program/ProgramStateCache.h`, `VK/VKProgramBuffer.h`, `VK/VKPresent.cpp`, `VK/VKRenderPass.cpp`, `VK/vkutils/descriptors.cpp`, `port_r2pipe.h`, `CMakeLists.txt` (+ `../fossilize`, Valve Fossilize, MIT) | Pipeline stutter round. `R2_VK_GPL` (default on when the device has `VK_EXT_graphics_pipeline_library` with `graphicsPipelineLibraryFastLinking`): a pipeline first needed during play is fast-linked from vertex-input / pre-rasterization / fragment-shader / fragment-output libraries (each cached by the exact bytes of its inputs) and the optimised monolithic pipeline (same create info as upstream) is compiled on the compiler thread when idle and swapped in atomically; program layouts use `INDEPENDENT_SETS`; the start-up preload stays monolithic. `R2_PRELOAD_ASYNC` (default 1 in the async shader mode, 0 otherwise): every shader is compiled before the first frame but only the `R2_PRELOAD_BOOT` (384) earliest-recorded pipelines are linked; `R2_PRELOAD_THREADS` (default cores/4, 1-4) low-priority threads link the rest during play; `0` = upstream blocking preload. `R2_FOSSILIZE`: `record` appends every pipeline (with its shaders, layouts, render pass) to `shaders_cache/<r2|r3>_pipelines.foz`; default `auto` replays that file, if present, on background threads into the shared `VkPipelineCache` after the RPCS3 preload (`replay` = also log when missing, `0` = off, `R2_FOSSILIZE_DB` = other path). `R2_PIPE_LOG` (default on): `[pipe]` line every 5 s with render-thread waits on shader/pipeline work and a >2 ms histogram. Upstream's per-thread `m_cache_miss_flag` is `thread_local`. |
+| `rpcs3/Emu/RSX/Common/texture_cache.h` (`upload_texture`) | Upstream fixes: `R2_TEX_UN3D_DEPTH` (default on, `0` = upstream). The unnormalized 3D/cubemap depth scale divides by the register depth instead of `attributes.depth`, which upstream still holds 0 at that point (infinite R scale). Same change as RPCS3 PR #19779 (unmerged); restores the R2 water ripples (RPCS3 issue #18250). |
+| `rpcs3/Emu/RSX/RSXThread.cpp` (flip), `RSXZCULL.cpp/.h` (`clear`) | Upstream fixes: `R2_ZCULL_FLIP_CLEAR` A/B for RPCS3 issue #18148 (missing objects with an uncapped frame rate). Unset/`1` = upstream flip-time ZCULL clear; `keep` = drain unclaimed reports but keep the running query (`clear(..., discard_active=false)`); `0` = no flip clear (query leak risk). Opt-in only. |
+| `RSXFIFO.cpp/.h`, `RSXOffload.cpp` | Renderer-thread round: `R2_FIFO_INLINE` (default on, `0` = upstream): `FIFO_control::fetch_u32_fast` inlines the cache-hit path of `fetch_u32` in `read_unsafe` and in `read`'s first-argument fetch; misses still call `fetch_u32`. `R2_DMA_INLINE_MAX=<bytes>` (default 65536, `0` = upstream 3584): `dma_manager::copy` copies inline up to this size instead of queueing to the Offloader (pushing into an empty queue costs a kernel wake). |
+
+## Not vendored / replaced (see `../rpcs3_shim`)
+
+- `rpcs3/Emu/RSX/GL/*`: excluded.
+- `rpcs3/Emu/System.cpp`: replaced by `emu_system_stub.cpp`.
+- `rpcs3/Emu/Memory/vm.cpp`: replaced by `vm_shim.cpp`.
+- `rpcs3/Emu/RSX/RSXRendererFactory.cpp`: replaced by `rsx_renderer_factory.cpp` (no GL).
+- NP overlays (friends, trophies, messages): excluded.
+- zlib, ffmpeg/swscale, wolfssl, git-version: shim headers in `rpcs3_shim/include`.
+- Vulkan loader: the import library is generated from `rpcs3_shim/vulkan/vulkan-1.def`; no SDK is needed at link time.
+
+Extra third-party code not in the RPCS3 submodule set:
+- `3rdparty/Vulkan-Headers` (v1.4.344)
+- `3rdparty/pugixml` (1.15)
+
+## Build (standalone)
+
+Run inside a VS 2022 x64 developer environment with LLVM on PATH:
+
+```
+cmake -S ps3recomp\third_party\rpcs3 -B build_rpcs3 -G Ninja -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=RelWithDebInfo -DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=clang-cl -DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=clang-cl
+cmake --build build_rpcs3 -j 8
+```
+
+Targets:
+- `rpcs3_rsx` (alias `rpcs3::rsx`): a static library.
+- `rpcs3_rsx_linktest`: a link check.
+
+The project can also be pulled in with `add_subdirectory(third_party/rpcs3)`.
+
+## Integration notes
+
+- The runtime must provide `extern "C" uint8_t* vm_base` and `vm_sudo_base`. `vm_sudo_base` is a second RW view of the same 4 GB.
+- Startup sequence:
+  1. Call `g_fxo->init()`, which resets and constructs the registered fxo objects.
+  2. Then call `rsx::create_render_thread(nullptr)`.
+  3. Set `g_emu_callbacks.get_gs_frame` before step 2.
+- `r2port::g_rsx_cache_dir` sets the shader cache dir. Leave it empty to disable the on-disk cache.
+- `rpcs3_shim/rsx_events_stub.cpp` holds `rsx::thread::send_event` and `sys_rsx_context_attribute`. Replace it with the real lv2 bridge.
