+		// RSX_DLSS_OBJMV_DEFORM_MB: history per frame (MB, two halves), RSX_DLSS_OBJMV_DEFORM_MAX: draws per frame.
+		bool om_deform = true;
+		u32 om_deform_mb = 16;
+		u32 om_deform_max = 96;
+		// RSX_AA_MATCH_LOOSE (default 1; 0 = strict keys only): a draw whose strict key (vertex program + vertex array 0 /
+		// index buffer addresses + ordinal) has no previous-frame match is paired by a loose key without buffer addresses
+		// (vertex program, fragment program, textures, vertex formats + ordinal). R3 builds its geometry on the SPU into
+		// a per-frame ring: the buffer addresses change every frame, so most draws never matched (no camera vote, no
+		// object motion, deformed meshes never seen twice). Non-indexed programs only; implausible pairs stay camera-only.
+		// 1: the key leaves out the fragment program address (R3 patches FP constants into per-draw ucode copies at
